# jobrunner

Small job runner with a configurable bounded retry policy.

## Retry policy

`run_job` preserves its public signature and accepts a `RetryConfig`, an
injected `Sleeper`, and a job closure. `max_attempts` is the total number of
calls, including the first call. Transient errors are retried with delays of
`base_delay_ms`, then twice that delay, and so on, capped at `max_delay_ms`.
Permanent errors are returned immediately, without sleeping. A zero
`max_attempts` value is treated as one attempt.

```rust
use jobrunner::{run_job, FakeSleeper, RetryConfig, RetryError};

let config = RetryConfig::new(3, 100, 500);
let mut sleeper = FakeSleeper::default();
let result = run_job(&config, &mut sleeper, || {
    Err(RetryError::Transient("temporary outage".into()))
});
assert!(result.is_err());
assert_eq!(sleeper.sleeps, vec![100, 200]);
```

